/-!
# The unchanged ordinary primary phase on the original source chart

The actual native event already reaches the retained global coefficient
threshold. The finite radial-carrier menu selects its joint derivative price
before every history, source row, source point and target order. The final
phase is literally `SampledQuadrature.group_phase` on the saved graph42.

`Native.P` has the fixed prehistory44 inputs. `Native.phase` has native51 inputs:
the saved reached proof mentions the actual original source row, although its
phase type and graph data close at native50. The original proof is retained.
The phase is smooth on the entire original chart23, with first derivative
bounded by `P 0` and every `(q+1)`-derivative bounded by
`P q * currentCoefficientScale^q`. `jets_of_le` increases only the slow scale
by a numerical inequality. The carrier is never doubled or shifted.

Consumer: `PhysicalPairs.SampledMask.first_mask` fields `hφ`, `hupper`, `hphase`
(`main:eq:primary-strain`, `app:ch_regular:eq:source-tail` in paper-v2).
The existing source geometry supplies the same `Ksource22` gradient condition.
-/
